# Portfolio Health & Reporting Architecture
A Data Analytics Capstone

📌 Overview
This project is a prototype of a bank‑grade portfolio reporting system.
It demonstrates how a financial institution can structure, calculate, and communicate the health of its loan portfolio using clean data models, transparent SQL, and executive‑ready visuals.

The goal: show end‑to‑end thinking — from raw data to insight.

📂 What’s Included
Data Model — normalized tables and analytical views

SQL Logic — modular, documented queries for every metric

Portfolio Health Metrics — composition, risk, concentrations, profitability

Officer Scorecard — production, quality, risk, and relationship value

Dashboards — executive‑grade Tableau visuals

Documentation — definitions, lineage, and governance

🎯 Key Features
1. Portfolio Composition
Loan counts, balances, exposure

Product, industry, and officer segmentation

Growth and runoff trends

2. Risk & Migration
Rating distribution

Year‑over‑year movement

Early‑warning indicators

3. Concentration Analysis
Industry

Geography

Officer

Product

4. Profitability
FTP allocation

RAROC

Relationship‑level contribution

5. Officer Scorecard
Production metrics

Portfolio quality

Risk management

Profitability impact

🧱 Data Architecture
Designed for clarity and auditability:

Staging → Clean → Analytical Views

Consistent naming conventions

Transparent calculation logic

Reusable components for future reporting

